  <name>Monti</name>
  <summary>Mount your clouds</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.stektus">
    <name>stektus</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Monti mounts Google Drive, Dropbox, OneDrive and other cloud storage
      as regular local folders on Linux. No terminal, no config files:
      install, click Add cloud, sign in through your browser — and your
      cloud appears as a folder. Open it in Dolphin, Nautilus, KeePassXC,
      LibreOffice — anything that works with files.
    </p>
    <p>
      Powered by the open-source rclone engine. Supports your own OAuth
      API key, per-drive cache options, read-only mounts, WebDAV/Nextcloud,
      S3-compatible storage and SFTP.
    </p>
  </description>
